WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.790
A bunch of shows are returning with new batches
of episodes - and of course, there's also

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:09.360
the usual eclectic selection of movies and
licensed TV series to help take your mind

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.849
off the late summer heat.

00:00:10.849 --> 00:00:15.040
Let's dig in to every notable new Netflix
viewing choice coming your way in August.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.120
Otherhood will come with a little extra baggage
when it drops August 2, but don't hold that

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.140
against it.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.800
One of its stars, Felicity Huffman, is one
of the celebrities caught up in the college

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.460
admissions scandal that's been headline news
lately.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.550
It's safe to say that Netflix is probably
hoping said scandal won't be at the forefront

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.670
of your mind when see the cast list.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:38.640
Otherhood stars Huffman, Angela Bassett, and
Patricia Arquette as a trio of moms who decide

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.440
to take a road trip to the Big Apple to reconnect
with their adult sons, making important discoveries

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.410
about their families, their friends, and themselves
along the way.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:50.170
The presence of the always-excellent Bassett
alone is enough to get our attention, and

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:54.519
the movie marks the directorial debut of Cindy
Chupack, who has worked as a writer and producer

00:00:54.519 --> 00:00:57.960
on TV series including Modern Family and Sex
and the City.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.629
The trailer promises a funny, heartfelt, and
moving little film that deserves a watch,

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.320
even if one of its stars isn't doing so hot
on the PR front this year.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:11.311
Dear White People has been a hilarious, thought-provoking
delight for its first two seasons, and for

00:01:11.311 --> 00:01:14.909
the third, debuting August 2, things are about
to get real.

00:01:14.909 --> 00:01:18.880
The series is a look at race relations from
the point of view of a group of black students

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.710
at a prestigious, mostly white fictional university.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:26.939
It stars Logan Browning as Sam, the host of
the titular radio show; DeRon Horton as Lionel,

00:01:26.939 --> 00:01:31.470
an aspiring journalist who has extra hurdles
to surmount as a gay man; and Antoinette Robertson

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:36.229
as Coco, a social butterfly attempting to
fit in to her lily-white environment.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:40.579
Previous seasons have focused on Sam and Lionel's
efforts to discover the identity of the mysterious

00:01:40.579 --> 00:01:46.009
leader of Order X, a shadowy secret society
- and at the conclusion of season 2, it was

00:01:46.009 --> 00:01:49.720
revealed to be the series' narrator, Giancarlo
Esposito.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:52.880
"I see you've been watching closely."

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:03.360
Esposito figures pretty heavily in the trailer
for season 3, so we can expect to learn more

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:06.200
about Order X along with Sam and Lionel.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.680
No Good Nick is among the weirdest sitcoms
on television, and we mean that in the best

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:11.700
way possible.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:16.380
Part 1 of the show's first season introduced
us to the oh-so average Thompson family: dad

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:21.390
Ed, mom Liz, son Jeremy, and daughter Molly,
who discover that they have a previously unknown,

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.970
distant relative: young Nick, whom they welcome
into their lives.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:30.000
But all is not as it seems: Nick is a budding
con artist, and in addition to putting over

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.380
a long con on the Thompsons, she's also playing
her foster parents in the service of a scheme

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.410
cooked up by her imprisoned father Tony.

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:41.530
Part 1 was equal parts hilarity, intrigue,
and suspense, and Part 2 promises to thicken

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:44.320
the plot even further when it debuts August
5.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.560
It's been a long wait for the third season
of GLOW, but the recently released trailer

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:53.370
for season 3 promises that it'll be worth
it when the season finally hits August 9.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:57.370
The new batch of episodes sees the action
move to Las Vegas, as the Gorgeous Ladies

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:01.780
of Wrestling take their act to the Fan-Tan
hotel and casino under the watchful eye of

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.200
an entertainment director played by Geena
Davis.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.200
"Viva Las Vegas."

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.680
Season 2 left plenty of plot threads to be
picked up, and star Alison Brie has teased

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:16.420
that the new outing will feature a deepening
of the friendship between her character Ruth

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:19.450
"Zoya the Destroya" Wilder and Debbie "Liberty
Belle" Eagan.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:24.470
The show's deft blend of comedy with thoughtful
explorations of unconventional relationships

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.240
has always been at the center of its appeal,
and the new season looks to give its fans

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.720
the most hilarious, heartfelt outing yet.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:35.630
Dexter's Michael C. Hall returns to the small
screen August 9 in the original feature In

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:39.740
the Shadow of the Moon, and he's just one
welcome component of the thriller's amazing

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:40.740
cast.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:44.970
Leading the film is Boyd Holbrook, who portrays
a Philadelphia police detective on the trail

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:49.541
of a serial killer whose crimes seem to defy
any logical explanation; Hall will appear

00:03:49.541 --> 00:03:53.390
as a fellow detective who is also the brother-in-law
of Holbrook's character.

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:58.840
The film is directed by Jim Mickle, who turned
in an amazingly atmospheric thriller in 2013's

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.290
We Are What We Are.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:04.530
Additional plot details are sparse, but something
tells us that's for the best, as this sounds

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:07.200
like a thriller best watched going in cold.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:12.440
The story of every '90s kid's favorite anxiety-ridden
wallaby continues with the feature Rocko's

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.110
Modern Life: Static Cling.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:18.980
The animated movie is going meta for its return:
Rocko and friends Heffer, Filburt and Spunky

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:24.210
have been lost in space since the Nickelodeon
series' conclusion in 1996, and they're going

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:27.540
to have a few problems adjusting to our radically
different modern world.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:32.360
Rocko, however, believes that this new society
can be redeemed through the power of nostalgia.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:36.580
See how our heroes react to smartphones, food
trucks, and superhero movies when Rocko's

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:39.670
Modern Life: Static Cling drops on August
9.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:43.120
"The 21st Century is a very dangerous century."

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:47.920
Invader Zim was one of the most insane offerings
ever fielded by Nickelodeon, and it amassed

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:51.990
a sizable fan base during its run from 2001
to 2006.

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:56.830
The animated series centered on Zim, an alien
from the planet Irk, and his attempts to conquer

00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:01.750
Earth with the aid of his not-so-reliable
robot assistant GIR; opposing them is Dib,

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:03.830
a pint-sized paranormal investigator.

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:07.810
Despite its relatively short run, the show
has remained popular, spawning its own fan

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:10.610
convention, a comic book series, and a plethora
of merchandise.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:15.690
Leave it to Netflix, then, to give fans a
feature film Invader Zim: Enter the Florpus!,

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.120
debuting August 16.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:21.720
Most of the original cast will return to reprise
their roles, including Richard Horvitz as

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:27.030
Zim, Rikki Simons as GIR, and Andy Berman
as Dib; series creator Jhonen Vasquez also

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:29.120
returned to co-script the project.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:33.440
Fans of the true crime drama series Mindhunter
have been waiting with bated breath for the

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:36.720
second season since the first arrived in 2017.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:41.230
On August 16, they'll finally get to see the
continuing story of FBI agents Holden Ford

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:45.600
and Bill Tench, who forged new methods of
capturing serial killers in the '70s.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:49.300
The pair are the first to interview such criminals
while in captivity to find out what makes

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:54.470
them tick, and the 1977-set first season saw
them cross paths with a number of real-life

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:57.970
monsters including the notorious "Co-Ed Killer"
Ed Kemper.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:02.050
Season 2 will take place after a bit of a
time jump, focusing on a rash of killings

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:06.430
in Atlanta which took place between 1979 and
1981.

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:10.030
In what is sure to be a highlight of the new
batch of episodes, Ford and Tench will have

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:13.400
occasion to interview infamous "family" leader
Charles Manson.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:18.550
If you've missed the comedy stylings of Marlon
Wayans, then Netflix has a movie just for

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:19.550
you.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:23.920
Sextuplets focuses on Alan, an adoptee who
hits the road in search of his birth mother,

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:28.120
only to discover that he was born a sextuplet,
and that he has five identical brothers.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:31.050
All of the brothers, of course, are played
by Wayans.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:35.800
The movie reunites Wayans with Bresha Webb,
the co-star of his short-lived sitcom Marlon,

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:39.870
and the film is directed by longtime Wayans
collaborator Michael Tiddes, who directed

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.670
A Haunted House and its sequel.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:45.730
Wayans is a man who knows what his audience
wants, and if you're a fan, you won't need

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:49.800
us to tell you to set aside August 16 to check
out Sextuplets.

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:53.240
Here's a little item that's been nearly four
decades in the making.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:58.750
The Dark Crystal: Age of Resistance is a series
serving as a prequel to Jim Henson's 1982

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:00.440
fantasy feature The Dark Crystal.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:04.660
The movie used pioneering puppet work to tell
the tale of a struggle to find a balance between

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:07.700
light and dark on the mysterious planet of
Thra.

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:12.139
Age of Resistance will follow the journey
of three Gelflings, voiced by Taron Egerton,

00:07:12.139 --> 00:07:16.350
Anya Taylor-Joy, and Nathalie Emmanuel, as
they set out to discover the secret behind

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.210
the power of the evil Skeksis.

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:23.000
The series blends the original's signature
puppetry with lovingly rendered CGI, and its

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:26.540
stellar voice cast includes nearly too much
talent to list.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:30.640
Even those unfamiliar with Henson's classic
film will want to get in on this one.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:34.240
As in July, the new action offerings are few
in August.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:38.320
Fortunately, they're all well worth checking
out; many consider Quentin Tarantino's Jackie

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.550
Brown to be among his finest works.

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:44.830
If you're more in the "mind-bending head trip"
mood, there's the Wachowskis' Jupiter Ascending,

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:49.900
a blast of pure, unadulterated sci-fi/action
craziness featuring Mila Kunis and Channing

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:50.900
Tatum.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:55.210
There's also 2004's The Punisher, featuring
Thomas Jane in his first go-round as the legendary

00:07:55.210 --> 00:08:00.170
Marvel anti-hero, the well-received Jason
Statham actioner The Bank Job, and Boyka:

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:03.640
Undisputed, the fourth film in the bone-crushing
martial arts series.

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:08.150
When it comes to horror, the August pickings
are, unfortunately, even slimmer.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:12.360
Only two new releases will show up during
the month: the ultra-crazy Daniel Radcliffe-led

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:17.540
Horns, and Panic Room, David Fincher's claustrophobic
thriller starring Jodie Foster as a woman

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:19.080
trapped in her own home.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:23.560
Sylvestor Stallone is the main attraction
among the August drama offerings, as the first

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:27.650
five films in the Rocky series will be available
for streaming on the first of the month.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:32.850
The 1994 classic Four Weddings and a Funeral
is also on tap, as well as the 1995 coming

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:38.539
of age drama Now and Then and the 1998 Frankie
Lymon biography Why Do Fools Fall in Love.

00:08:38.539 --> 00:08:42.890
On the 20th, check out one of the great Daniel
Day-Lewis performances as the ruthless gang

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:46.240
leader "Bill the Butcher" in Martin Scorsese's
Gangs of New York.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:51.560
The new comedy offerings for August are graced
by one classic standout: Groundhog Day, which

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:55.940
stars Bill Murray as a man forced to relive
the same day over and over again until he

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:56.940
gets it right.

00:08:56.940 --> 00:09:00.990
You can also catch Ice Cube's Are We Done
Yet?, the Sex and the City movie, the Jack

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:05.490
Nicholson/Diane Keaton vehicle Something's
Gotta Give, and the hilarious Anna Faris starring

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:06.500
in The House Bunny.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:10.560
And if none of these are quite weird enough
for you, there's To Wong Foo, Thanks for Everything!

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:15.450
Julie Newmar, which features Wesley Snipes,
John Leguizamo, and Patrick Swayze as three

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:18.840
drag queens who embark on the most bizarre
road trip ever.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:24.360
Aside from the ones already listed, new TV
seasons are a bit few and far between in August.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:28.400
The second season of riveting crime series
The Sinner, focusing on the brutal crimes

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:31.100
committed by a young boy, comes to Netflix
in August.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:35.320
The CW's Jane the Virgin will see its fifth
season added to the service, and the second

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:39.779
season of the History Channel's 14th century
drama Knightfall will also be available.

00:09:39.779 --> 00:09:45.360
Finally, season 6 of the CW's sci-fi drama
The 100 will join the lineup on August 14.

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:50.400
Original comedy offerings kick off with Volume
4 of Patriot Act with Hasan Minhaj, in which

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:55.260
the comedian uses sly humor to deliver biting
social commentary on the state of the U.S.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:57.790
in today's divisive political climate.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:02.790
Also appearing are solo sets from veteran
standup Sebastian Maniscalco and director/comedian

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:03.790
Simon Amstell.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:08.420
Finally, Tiffany Haddish Presents: They Ready,
will put the spotlight on six budding comedians

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:10.700
performing half-hour sets.

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:12.820
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:16.330
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:19.499
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

